  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Integrated financial management of climate risks in the agricultural sector in Peru</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project advised the Peruvian Ministry of Agriculture (MINAGRI) on establishing a risk-transfer system with the backing of both the state and the private sector. The system improved food security, enhanced economic stability in rural areas and helped the agricultural sector to better cope with climate change. The private and public financial services offered through the system enabled agricultural producers to reduce their vulnerability to weather extremes - which were exacerbated by climate change - and to limit their exposure to the associated risks. The project was supporting the development of an information system and strengthening the expertise required for the management and government supervision of risk transfer systems in Peru.</narrative>
  </description>
